* text=auto eol=lf
*.kspl text eol=lf
*.ksplb text eol=lf
*.kspeg text eol=lf
*.c text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# GitHub highlights KSPL with Rust's grammar (not a Linguist language), the parser's brace fixtures
# (`*.ksplb`) too.
*.kspl linguist-language=Rust
*.ksplb linguist-language=Rust
# Caution: **Keep git off the `embed` samples**: a converted line end leaves nothing to compare.
ksplc/tests/prog/embed_data/* -text
# The seed is generated (`make commit-seed`): a re-bake rewrites 7 MB, which floods a diff and that
# GitHub will not render. **`-diff` hides only the text**: `git diff --text` still shows it, and
# merging is untouched.
ksplc/seed.c linguist-generated=true -diff
